# 3-Site Full-Mesh OSPF (Area 0) Enterprise Network

referrence simulation file packet tracer
https://drive.google.com/file/d/1uR_Qrx9i09_7lIegEVGguxXcQHIRALW2/view?usp=sharing

A beginner-to-intermediate OSPF lab simulating three branch sites (Site A, Site B, Site C), 
each running Router-on-a-Stick VLAN segmentation, interconnected via a full-mesh OSPF single-area 
(Area 0) topology.

---

## 📐 Topology

```
                         R1 (Site C)
                        /            \
                 10.0.12.0/30      10.0.13.0/30
                      /                  \
                 R2 (Site A) ---------- R3 (Site B)
                          10.0.23.0/30
```

| Router | Site | Fa0/0 | Fa0/1 | Eth1/0 (Trunk to Core Switch) |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| R1 | Site C | 10.0.12.1/30 (→ R2) | 10.0.13.1/30 (→ R3) | Subinterfaces .50 / .60 |
| R2 | Site A | 10.0.12.2/30 (→ R1) | 10.0.23.1/30 (→ R3) | Subinterfaces .10 / .20 |
| R3 | Site B | 10.0.13.2/30 (→ R1) | 10.0.23.2/30 (→ R2) | Subinterfaces .30 / .40 |

Each router is connected to a Core Switch via a trunk link (`Eth1/0`), which
distributes VLANs down to access switches and end devices. Native VLAN 100 is used for 
trunking on all sites.

